# HYUNJUN — "One More Stop"
# Seoul at night: Line 2, convenience stores, bus stops, street lamps doubled in puddles.
# Theme: not wanting good moments to end -> an ending does not erase what happened.
# Seed: var.snack (kimbap / banana / icecream), set in hyunjun_intro.
# Geography (real Line 2 order): ... Ewha > Sinchon > Hongik Univ. > Hapjeong > [Han River bridge]
#   > Dangsan > Yeongdeungpo-gu Office > Mullae > Sindorim (transfer). Past ride and dawn ride share this stretch.

=== hyunjun_intro
@show hyunjun laugh at=c
@cam closeup hyunjun
> Hyunjun is perched on the arm of a sofa with a convenience-store bag in his lap.
> The bag is damp, stretched thin, and carrying more than any bag was designed for.
hyunjun: {{playerName}}! Good. You can be the judge.
hyunjun[smile]: Justin says I panic-bought. I say I *prepared*. The difference is attitude.
> He opens it like a treasure chest. Triangle kimbap. Banana milk. Ice cream bars, sweating politely through their wrappers.
you: How many convenience stores did you stop at?
hyunjun: Three! They're all different. The one by the bridge has the good kimbap. The one by the bus stop has a cat.
hyunjun[thinking]: The third one I went into because it was there. That's a valid reason.
@show justin smile at=r
justin: He bought for nine people before he knew there *were* nine people.
hyunjun: I always buy for one more than there is. Somebody always turns up.
hyunjun[laugh]: And look! Somebody turned up.
> Justin lifts a banana milk out of the bag without asking, stabs the straw in, and drifts off toward the front desk.
@hide justin
hyunjun: That's theft. I'm keeping a record. Anyway — pick one before he comes back.
* [sincere] A triangle kimbap.
    @var snack = "kimbap"
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[smile]: Tuna mayo. The correct answer. I bought other flavours in case people were wrong.
    > One corner is slightly squashed. He apologises to the kimbap, not to you.
* [playful] A banana milk. "Before Justin drinks them all."
    @var snack = "banana"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Yes. Thank you. Somebody in this building understands the stakes.
    > He hands it over like a classified document.
* [quiet] An ice cream bar, rain or not.
    @var snack = "icecream"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[surprised]: Ice cream. In the rain. At one in the morning.
    hyunjun[smile]: Okay. Respect. That's a person who does what they want.
hyunjun: This is the best night. A building that *talks*. I've been waiting my whole life for a building to talk.
you: Did you send something to it? A record?
hyunjun[thinking]: I think so. A video. Of the subway. Mostly the windows.
hyunjun[laugh]: Sixteen-year-old me thought he was a film director. Eleven minutes of windows. Very artistic. Very long.
> He laughs, and then his eyes go to the Archive Wall, to the hundreds of glowing boxes, and stay there a beat too long.
hyunjun: It said *deleted*. At five.
hyunjun[smile]: Which is fine! Five is ages away. And after five there's breakfast, and after breakfast there's a place by the river that opens at seven, and—
you: And after that?
hyunjun: After that I'll think of something. There's always one more thing.
* [sincere] "You really don't want tonight to end."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    > For a second he's completely quiet. It doesn't look like him at all. It also looks more like him than anything so far.
    hyunjun: ...Good nights don't come around that often. You have to hold on with both hands.
    hyunjun[smile]: Also I have snacks for at least six more hours. It'd be a waste.
* [playful] "What if I get tired?"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Then we find somewhere to sit with a view. Sitting with a view counts as a place.
    hyunjun: I have a list. I add to it faster than I cross things off.
* [quiet] Nod, and open your snack.
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[smile]: Yeah. Eat first. Plans after. That's the right order.
hyunjun: I'm going to give you a nickname, by the way. I'm working on it. They take a while. They have to be earned.
you: What's Justin's?
hyunjun: Thief.
> Across the lobby, a straw slurps loudly, in protest.
@hub act1

=== hyunjun_intro_repeat
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: Back for seconds? There's plenty. Justin's only been through the bag twice.
> The bag is noticeably lighter than it was ten minutes ago.
hyunjun[laugh]: Three times. I just watched him. Go, save yourself, take a kimbap.
@hub act1

=== hyunjun_door
@bg studio_hall t=fade
@show hyunjun thinking at=c
> Hyunjun is walking the length of the hall. Door to window. Window to door. His sneakers squeak on every turn.
you: How many laps is that?
hyunjun: Fourteen. Fifteen? I lost count around the fire extinguisher.
hyunjun[smile]: I think better walking. If I stand still, my brain stands still too and just goes *hmm*.
> He stops in front of the fifth door. Its number glows a soft pink, as if it knew what colour to be.
hyunjun: It's the train. I know it's the train. I remember what I sent.
hyunjun[thinking]: It's weird. I've wanted to watch that video again for years. I couldn't. I mailed away the only copy, like an idiot. Like a *poet*.
hyunjun: And now it's right there, and I've done fifteen laps instead of opening it.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 05 is ready. The owner has walked 340 metres in this corridor tonight. I am not in a hurry.
@textbox normal
hyunjun[laugh]: See? Even the building thinks I'm stalling.
hyunjun[smile]: Okay. It's mine, and I'm saying yes. Yes. I want to see it.
hyunjun: But you do the door. If I do it, it turns into one more lap.
* "Open it."
    hyunjun[laugh]: Okay. Okay! The doors are closing. Please watch your step.
    @sfx door
    @goto hyunjun_room
* "Not yet."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Oh, thank goodness. I mean — that's fine. That's so fine.
    hyunjun[smile]: One more lap, then. You can come. It's a really good hallway.
    > He says it as a joke. He also gives you the inside lane.
    @hub act2

=== hyunjun_room
@bg mem_subway t=memory
@music hyunjun
@amb subway
@fx memory n=0.5
@sfx train
@cam reveal
> The door opens on a subway car.
> Not a set. Not a picture on a wall. A whole car, rocking gently on rails that aren't there.
> It hums at the exact pitch of every late train you've ever been too tired on.
> Fluorescent light. Green seats worn shiny. An advert for a dental clinic that promises to change your life.
> Every window is black. Every window is a mirror.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 05 — OWNER: HYUNJUN. TYPE: VIDEO. DURATION: 11 MINUTES, 40 SECONDS.
echo: DATE: DECEMBER, FOUR YEARS AGO. 23:51. LINE 2, LAST TRAIN. UNRESOLVED SUBJECTS: 1.
@textbox normal
@show hyunjun surprised at=c
hyunjun: Oh.
hyunjun: Oh, it's the *car*. It's the actual— there's the rip in the seat! Somebody fixed it with tape. I remember the tape!
> He walks the length of the car before you've taken three steps. Touches the pole. Reads the dental advert out loud. Walks back.
hyunjun[laugh]: Sorry. I have to walk it. I can't just *look* at it.
@if rooms() == 0
    > Across the aisle, at the end of the bench, something is sitting where a passenger should be.
    > A shape made of soft light. Knees drawn up. Head turned toward the window.
    hyunjun[thinking]: That's the unresolved thing. The one ECHO keeps talking about.
    hyunjun: That's where they sat. The person I talked to.
    > He says *the person* the way you'd say the name of a town you only drove through once.
@elif rooms() >= 4
    > Across the aisle, at the end of the bench, the silhouette of light is sitting exactly where you knew it would be.
    hyunjun[laugh]: Okay. At this point I'd be *shocked* if it wasn't you.
    hyunjun[smile]: Don't tell me. I want to find out properly. I want the whole episode.
@else
    > Across the aisle, at the end of the bench, a silhouette of light sits with its knees drawn up, watching the window.
    hyunjun[thinking]: The glowing person. They've been in the other rooms too, right?
    hyunjun: Is it you again?
    > He asks it lightly. He doesn't quite look at you when he does.
    hyunjun[smile]: Don't answer. Let's watch. I'm really good at being surprised. It's one of my skills.
hyunjun: Okay. Honestly. What do you think? I know it's just a subway car.
* [playful] "Ten out of ten. The dental advert ties it all together."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: *Right?* He's been smiling at me for four years. I never found out if the life change worked.
* [sincere] "It looks like somewhere you were happy."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[surprised]: ...Yeah.
    hyunjun[smile]: Yeah, I was. Weird place for it. Line 2 at midnight. Everybody else is just trying to get home.
* [quiet] Sit down on the taped seat.
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    > The tape crinkles under you. It sounds exactly the way it should.
    hyunjun[surprised]: That's my seat. That was *my* seat. You just sat in my seat.
    hyunjun[laugh]: No, stay. You're doing it right. That's where the good reflection is.
> Out of habit, he lifts his phone to the nearest window. In the black glass, his reflection lifts a phone back.
hyunjun[laugh]: Muscle memory. Four years, and my arm still knows the angle.
hyunjun: ECHO? Can I see it? The video part. The— me part.
@textbox echo
echo: Playing RECORD 05. Please hold on to the handrails. That is a joke. There is no motion.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@textbox memory
@fx snow n=0.3
> The car flickers. Another passenger fades into being, halfway down the bench.
> Sixteen. Black hair — no pink yet, not for years. A school coat zipped to the chin. A phone held flat against the window.
> He isn't filming the tunnel. He's filming the glass, where the inside of the train floats over the dark like a second train.
> Across the aisle, the silhouette of light. Somebody else who hasn't got off.
hyunjun: Sorry. Am I in your— no, are *you* in my shot. Is that okay? I can move.
you: What are you filming?
hyunjun: The windows. At night they turn into mirrors. The whole city's out there, and all you get is the inside of the train.
hyunjun: I think it's cool. I haven't decided yet if it's cool.
you: It's a little cool.
hyunjun: Okay. Then it's cool. You're the tiebreaker.
you: Where are you getting off?
hyunjun: I'm not. I'm riding it round. It's a circle. It has to bring me back eventually.
> He digs in his coat pocket and comes out with a triangle kimbap, flattened at one corner.
hyunjun: Want half? I sat on it. It's still good. Structurally it's fine.
> He tears it down the middle without waiting for an answer and holds one half across the aisle. The silhouette takes it.
> A chime. A calm recorded voice, in Korean and then in English. *This stop is Hapjeong.*
hyunjun: Is this yours?
you: Not yet.
> The doors open on an empty platform. Close again. Two reflections sway together in the dark glass.
hyunjun: One more stop?
you: One more stop.
> Then the train climbs out of the ground, onto the bridge, and for one minute the windows stop being mirrors.
> The river underneath is black and full of lights. Snow is falling into it without making a sound.
you: Bye, river.
hyunjun: ...Did you just say bye to the river?
you: We're moving tomorrow. I'm riding it one last time. Saying all the names. One more time each.
hyunjun: That's so sad. That's so— no. That's sad *and* great. Both.
hyunjun: I've been here four months. I don't even know how to say hi to it yet.
you: You're doing it. That's what the windows are.
> He looks at his phone, then at the glass, like somebody just answered a question he hadn't finished asking.
> Dangsan. Yeongdeungpo-gu Office. Mullae. At every stop the doors open, he looks across, he asks. At every stop the answer is yes.
> Then the chime again. *This stop is Sindorim. You can transfer to Line 1.*
> The silhouette stands up.
you: This one's mine.
hyunjun: Wait— already? One more—
you: I can't. I have to change here. Thanks for the stops.
> The doors open. The figure steps out onto the platform, turns, lifts one hand.
hyunjun: Wait, what's your—
> The doors close on the end of the sentence.
> In the window, for one second, there are still two reflections. Then there is one.
@fx memory n=0.5
@textbox normal
> You know this.
> Not the way you know a story. The way you know a staircase in the dark.
> The last train. The night before the moving truck. A kid in a school coat asking the same question at every stop, until it stopped being a question.
@show hyunjun sad at=c
@cam closeup hyunjun
hyunjun: That's it. That's where it ends.
hyunjun: I stayed on till the end of the line. And I never found out—
* [sincere] "Hyunjun. That was me."
    @rel hyunjun trust+2
    > It comes out plainer than you meant. There isn't a fancier way to say it.
* [quiet] Stand up. Walk to where the silhouette stood. Let the window show him.
    @rel hyunjun trust+1 closeness+1
    > You stop at the door, where the figure turned. In the black glass, your reflection settles into the exact place the light was.
    > It fits like a key.
* [playful] "You never did get my name. It's {{playerName}}. For the record."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+2
    > Somewhere in the ceiling, ECHO makes a small noise, like somebody writing something down.
@show hyunjun surprised at=c
hyunjun: ...
hyunjun: Wait.
hyunjun: *Wait.*
> He looks at you. At the window. At you in the window. His mouth opens and nothing comes out of it, which, you are beginning to understand, is rare.
hyunjun[laugh]: You're *Sindorim*.
you: I'm what?
hyunjun: I called you Sindorim. In my head. For four years. I didn't have a name, so I used the station!
you: You named me after a transfer station.
hyunjun: It's a great station! It's huge! It has a department store! It's a compliment!
hyunjun[surprised]: Oh my gosh. You ate half my squashed kimbap. That was *you*.
you: It was structurally fine.
hyunjun[laugh]: It WAS structurally fine! I've been defending that kimbap for four years!
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 05 — UNRESOLVED SUBJECT: RESOLVED. Thank you. I have updated four years of notes.
echo: I had been filing them under "Sindorim." I will change that.
@textbox normal
hyunjun[laugh]: ECHO, *no*. You too?
> He's laughing, and then, somewhere in the middle of it, he isn't.
> He sits down hard on the taped seat, like his legs made the decision for him.
hyunjun[thinking]: Sorry. Give me a second. I'm doing math. Four years. You were *right there* the whole time. Not right there. Somewhere. But real.
* [sincere] "I remember the tape on this seat. I remember the snow on the river."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[surprised]: You remember the *tape*?
    hyunjun[smile]: Nobody remembers the tape. I thought I made the tape up.
* [playful] "Real, and apparently a department store."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: A *great* department store. With a food court. I'm not taking it back.
* [careful] Sit beside him and wait until he's ready.
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    > He doesn't take a second. He takes about thirty. You don't hurry him. The car hums.
    hyunjun[smile]: ...Thanks. I'm ready. I think. Mostly.
hyunjun: Can I tell you the dumb part?
hyunjun[thinking]: The next morning, it was like it never happened.
hyunjun: There was nothing. No name. A video of windows, and one reflection that could have been anybody.
hyunjun: I tried telling people. It came out like nothing. "I rode a train with someone." Okay? And?
hyunjun: So I walked home. From the end of the line. The whole way, till the first train. Because if I got home, it was over.
> He says it lightly, the way people say the heavy things when they've been carrying them long enough to know the weight by heart.
hyunjun[smile]: And then I just — kept doing it. Anything good, I stay. One more place. One more stop. One more minute.
hyunjun[laugh]: I'm a nightmare to leave anywhere with. Ask anyone. Songha has a system for getting me out of restaurants.
* [playful] "Songha has a *system*?"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Three warnings. Then he picks up my jacket and walks out. I follow the jacket. It works every time. I hate it.
* [sincere] "Does it work? Making things not end?"
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[thinking]: ...No.
    hyunjun: Everything ends anyway. I just get more tired first.
* [quiet] "You walked all night?"
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[smile]: Four hours. My feet were destroyed. I found eleven convenience stores. It was, honestly, a great night. Just — sad-great.
hyunjun: Can I ask you something? You said "we're moving" like you'd said it a lot.
* [sincere] "A lot. I got good at goodbyes. Trains were how I did them."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    you: One last ride. All the names. Then you're allowed to go.
* [quiet] "I was always the one who got off."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1 closeness+1
    > You've never said it that simply before. It sounds truer out loud than it did in your head.
* [playful] "I've said goodbye to more cities than I've unpacked in. I'm a professional."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: That's the saddest brag I've ever heard. I love it.
hyunjun[thinking]: So I'm the one who never gets off. And you're the one who always does.
hyunjun: That's a terrible pair. We'd never get anywhere.
hyunjun[smile]: Or — no. We'd get *everywhere*. One of us just complains the whole time.
> Outside the windows, a station slides past that isn't on any map. Just light, and a platform, and nobody waiting on it.
hyunjun: This is going to end too, isn't it. The room. The video's eleven minutes forty. We're way over.
* [romantic] Sit close enough that the window holds both of you. {if hyunjun.closeness >= 2 or hyunjun.trust >= 2}
    @rel hyunjun romance+1
    > You move over. Not all the way. Just until the dark glass across the aisle shows two people instead of one and a gap.
    hyunjun[shy]: ...Oh. There. That's the shot.
    hyunjun: That's the one I was trying to get. Four years ago. I just didn't know it had to be from this side.
* [romantic] "Ask me. The thing you always ask." {if hyunjun.trust >= 2}
    @rel hyunjun romance+1
    hyunjun[surprised]: One more—
    > He stops. Laughs at himself, softly.
    hyunjun[shy]: No. You'd say yes. And then I'd never learn anything.
* [sincere] "It's still going. We've got a few minutes."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[smile]: A few minutes. Okay. I can do a lot with a few minutes. I've been training for this.
> The fluorescent lights stutter. The car's hum drops half a note, the way trains do right before the last stop.
hyunjun[thinking]: Okay. It's going to stop. I'm going to be normal about it. I'm going to be so normal.
* [romantic] Take hold of his sleeve. "Then we'll be normal about it together." {if hyunjun.romance >= 1}
    @rel hyunjun romance+1
    > The bomber jacket is cold and a little slippery. You hold on anyway.
    > He looks down at your hand, then very carefully doesn't move his arm at all, like there's a bird on it.
    hyunjun[shy]: ...Yeah. Okay. Together. That's — yeah.
* [playful] "You're about to ask ECHO for an encore."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: I am *not*— ECHO, can it play one more—
    @textbox echo
    echo: No.
    @textbox normal
    hyunjun[laugh]: Wow. Okay. Fair.
* [quiet] Stay beside him until the lights go out.
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    > Neither of you says anything. It's not the silence of having nothing to say. It's the other kind.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 05 has ended. Thank you for riding.
echo: That is what the train says. I have always wanted to say it.
@textbox normal
@fx off
> The car goes still. The windows stay dark. The taped seat stays taped.
hyunjun: Hey. Can I say it? Your name.
hyunjun: I've been waiting four years to have one to say.
* [romantic] "Say it." {if hyunjun.romance >= 1 or hyunjun.closeness >= 3}
    @rel hyunjun romance+1
    hyunjun: {{playerName}}.
    > No nickname. No exclamation mark. Just your name, set down carefully, like something he'd been carrying the whole way.
* [sincere] "It's yours. Go ahead."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun: {{playerName}}.
    hyunjun[smile]: Huh. It's better than Sindorim. Don't tell Sindorim.
* [playful] "Only if I get to keep 'Sindorim' as a backup."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Deal. {{playerName}}. And Sindorim, for emergencies.
hyunjun[smile]: It happened. It really happened. I have *proof* now.
hyunjun: ...Okay. Let's go before I start doing laps in here.
@flag room_hyunjun
@unlock memory:hyunjun
@autosave
@goto hub_after_room

=== hyunjun_hub
@show hyunjun smile at=c
@if flag.room_hyunjun and not flag.hyunjun_postchat
    > Hyunjun is doing laps of the lobby, eating a triangle kimbap as he walks. He sees you and changes course mid-step.
    hyunjun: Sindo— {{playerName}}! Sorry. Retraining my brain. Four years of habit.
    @show justin thinking at=r
    justin: Why is he calling you a subway station?
    hyunjun: It's a long story.
    justin: It's a short story. You told me in March. You rode a train with somebody.
    hyunjun[laugh]: It was a *long train*.
    justin[surprised]: Wait. Wait, the train person? *That* train person?
    > Justin looks at you. Then at Hyunjun. Then he quietly takes the other half of the kimbap out of Hyunjun's hand, as if to mark the occasion.
    justin[smile]: Congratulations. I'm taking this as a fee.
    @hide justin
    hyunjun: He does that. Every time something good happens to me, I lose a snack.
    hyunjun[thinking]: It's weird. I keep checking that it's still true. Like I'll turn around and it'll have gone.
    hyunjun[smile]: It hasn't. You're still here. I checked four times.
    > He rummages in the bag, finds the last whole kimbap, and tears it in half without asking whether you want some.
    hyunjun: Half. It's a policy now. I split things with people from trains.
    * [playful] "You can keep calling me Sindorim."
        @rel hyunjun closeness+1
        hyunjun[laugh]: Really? No. No, I'll save it. For special occasions. Birthdays. Emergencies.
    * [romantic] "I'm glad it was you on that train." {if hyunjun.romance >= 1}
        @rel hyunjun romance+1
        hyunjun[shy]: ...
        hyunjun[shy]: You can't just *say* that while I'm holding half a kimbap.
        hyunjun[smile]: Me too, though. Obviously. I'm glad it was you. Me too.
    * [quiet] Take the half. Eat it next to him.
        @rel hyunjun trust+1
        > The seaweed has gone soft. Neither of you mentions it. For a whole minute, he doesn't walk anywhere.
    @flag hyunjun_postchat
@elif flag.room_hyunjun
    @if rooms() >= 6
        hyunjun: Look at you. Almost every room. You get around. You're like Line 2.
        hyunjun[smile]: That's a compliment. It's the best line. It goes everywhere and comes back.
    @else
        hyunjun: Still here! Good. I keep checking.
        > He pretends to count you, the way a teacher counts heads on a field trip. He gets to one and looks pleased with it.
@else
    > Hyunjun is sitting on the stairs with the snack bag between his feet, guarding it with his knees.
    hyunjun: I'm defending the bag. Justin's circling. He thinks I can't see him. I can see him.
    hyunjun[thinking]: Have you been in any rooms yet? What's it like? Is it weird? Is it good-weird?
    you: Good-weird, mostly.
    hyunjun[smile]: Okay. Good-weird I can do.
    hyunjun: Mine's the train. You'll know it when you see it. The door's pink. I didn't even ask it to be.
    > Behind him, a hand reaches silently between the banisters and removes a banana milk from the bag.
    hyunjun[laugh]: JUSTIN.
@hub act2

=== hyunjun_route
@chapter route
@time 03:50
@var route = "hyunjun"
@bg studio_ext_night t=slow d=2
@fx off
@amb city
@music quiet
@cam reveal
> The rain stopped hours ago. It left everything behind it: puddles in the alley, a shine on the brick, every street lamp doubled.
> The laundromat is still open. One dryer turns slowly, full of somebody's towels, going nowhere.
> Hyunjun is walking in circles around the biggest puddle.
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: Oh! You came out. Hi. I'm not being weird. I'm doing laps.
you: Around a puddle?
hyunjun: It's a very good puddle. It has a whole street lamp in it. Look.
> It does. A perfect lamp, upside down, trembling a little every time a drip lands in it.
hyunjun[thinking]: Inside, ECHO keeps saying numbers. Seventy minutes. Sixty-eight minutes. Every time it says one, I want to go buy snacks.
hyunjun: So I came out here where the numbers can't get me.
hyunjun[laugh]: The dryer has watched me go past eleven times. I think it's worried about me.
* [playful] "Should I be worried about you?"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: Only a normal amount. The dryer's being dramatic.
* [sincere] "I came to find you."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[surprised]: You— out of everybody?
    hyunjun[shy]: Okay. Okay, cool. I'm going to be calm about that. Watch me be calm.
* [quiet] Stand at the edge of the puddle beside him.
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    > In the water, the street lamp gets company. Two shapes lean into its light, wobbling whenever the wind moves.
    hyunjun[smile]: See? It's better with two. It's always better with two.
hyunjun: Walk with me? Just around the block.
hyunjun[thinking]: Or — the convenience store. It's two blocks. It's the one with the cat.
hyunjun: I know. I know I'm doing it. I'm aware I'm doing the thing. Come anyway?
* [playful] "Is the cat even awake at four a.m.?"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: The cat *works* nights. The cat is a professional. Like us.
